    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12">

                <pb facs="0015" n="9" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg9"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859A.20/184: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iceland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reykjavik</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-19T11:00:00+00:00">May 19, 1942—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:09 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>259. Department’s 136, May 15, 6 p.m. In a communication<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d12-f1"/> which I handed to the Prime Minister<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d12-f2"/> yesterday morning, I informed him that our exchange of
                    notes might be considered as constituting an agreement provided it is understood
                    (1) that no discrimination against the interests of the United States will be
                    rendered possible by the not granting to its nationals and aviation interests at
                    this time of equal treatment with Icelandic nationals and aviation interests;
                    and (2) that ill his stipulation that no future military commitments shall be
                    entered into in connection with the undertakings of the United States military
                    forces here, the word “future” applies only to the period after the war.</p>
                <pb facs="0016" n="10" xml:id="pg10"/>
                <p>Mr. Thors at once stated verbally afternoon conformed in writing, that the
                    Icelandic Government’s understanding of the above two points conforms with ours
                    as stated, and he has now ordered the issuance of the necessary proclamation
                    establishing the restricted area at Keflavik.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d12-f1" n="10" xml:id="d12-f1-content">
